# Line-ending contract (factory hardening round, item 7a — defect D-C2-1).
#
# The repository is stored with LF and must be CHECKED OUT with LF on every
# host, including Windows hosts with `core.autocrlf=true`. A CRLF checkout
# breaks Vite's SSR transform: its hashbang regexp /^#!.*\n/ only matches an
# LF-terminated shebang, so a CRLF shebang survives the transform, the
# imported module fails to parse and vitest collects 0 tests instead of
# running the suite.
#
# `text=auto` keeps git's own binary detection, `eol=lf` forces LF in the
# working tree. This file changes attribute resolution ONLY — it does not
# rewrite a single tracked blob (the index already stores LF for all of them).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The db-bootstrap fixture carries intentional NUL bytes (SQLite header):
# it must stay binary and must never be line-ending normalised — not even by
# an explicit `git add --renormalize .`.
tests/unit/db-bootstrap.test.mjs -text
